@nidhijaju Thanks for the PR. This is a great suggestion. Just a style consideration (trying to not use references as nouns).

> The DNS specification {{Section 3.2.1 of !RFC1035}} states that DNS records with a TTL of zero "can only be used for > the transaction in progress, and should not be cached". This document does not change that guidance;

Would the proposed text be ok with you?

> @gakiwate as discussed, adding a Firefox section. Depends on [mozilla/happy-eyeballs#125](https://github.com/mozilla/happy-eyeballs/issues/125) and Happy Eyeballs v3 landing in Firefox Release ([tracking issue](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1953459)). I expect this to happen soon, i.e. before this draft publishes.

All pending work is now merged into Firefox, i.e. this pull request is ready to merge from my end.

@gakiwate @StuartCheshire could you give this patch a review?
